### Section 9 $expand examples (local mock users). Status codes are single letters, e.g. 'A'.
@catalog = http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/catalog
@um = http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/user-management

### Travellers with locations and destinations
GET {{catalog}}/Travellers?$expand=locations($expand=destination)
Authorization: Basic admin:admin

### Select only specific fields
GET {{catalog}}/Travellers?$select=ID,firstName,lastName,fullName,status_code&$expand=locations($select=travelFrom,travelTo,notes;$expand=destination($select=name,country,city))
Authorization: Basic admin:admin

### Active travellers with locations from 2026
GET {{catalog}}/Travellers?$filter=status_code eq 'A'&$expand=locations($filter=travelFrom ge 2026-01-01)
Authorization: Basic admin:admin

### Own locations with destination
GET {{catalog}}/TravelledLocations?$expand=destination($select=name,country,city,region)&$orderby=travelFrom desc
Authorization: Basic aarav.sharma:aarav

### Location with traveller and destination
GET {{catalog}}/TravelledLocations?$top=1&$expand=traveller($select=firstName,lastName,fullName),destination
Authorization: Basic admin:admin

### Users with roles
GET {{um}}/Users?$expand=roles($expand=role)
Authorization: Basic admin:admin

### Lock a user
GET {{um}}/lockUser(userId=e5afc317-318d-5084-a335-28ff0fee11b1)
Authorization: Basic admin:admin

### Create a user
POST {{um}}/createUser
Authorization: Basic admin:admin
Content-Type: application/json

{ "firstName": "Ann", "lastName": "Lee", "email": "ann.lee@example.com", "roleId": "AGENT" }
